    "lawCode": "Add §§209-G & 630-b, Tax L; add §99-q, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4982\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the tax law and the state finance\nlaw, in relation to establishing the volunteer firefighting and\nvolunteer emergency services recruitment and retention fund and\nauthorizing gifts to such fund through a state income tax check-off\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :  This bill would make it easy to\nvoluntarily contribute to a fund to be used to help enhance\nrecruitment and retention efforts for volunteer firefighters and\nvolunteer emergency workers.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :  Section 1 amends the tax law by\nadding a new section 209-G to enable tax payers to make a contribution\nto the volunteer firefighting and volunteer emergency services\nrecruitment and retention fund.\n\nSection 2 amends article 22 of the Tax law creating a new \"tax check\noff\" on the New York State Income tax form to make it convenient to\ngive a gift to the volunteer firefighters and volunteer emergency\nservices recruitment and retention fund. Contributing to the fund does\nnot reduce taxes owed to the state.\n\nSection 3 adds a new section 99-q to the State Finance Law creating\nthe volunteer firefighters and volunteer emergency services\nrecruitment and retention fund in the joint custody of the\nCommissioner of Tax and Finance and the Comptroller. Authorizes\nexpenditures from the fund for grants to volunteer firefighters and\nvolunteer emergency service organizations for the purpose of\nencouraging the recruitment and retention of volunteer firefighters\nand volunteer emergency service personnel.\n\nThis section also declares that to the extent Possible, the Secretary\nof the State shall ensure that all monies received during a fiscal\nyear are expended prior to the end of that fiscal year.\n\nSection 4 provides that the act take effect 180 days after it becomes\na law.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :  Volunteer firefighters and volunteer emergency\nservices workers are crucial to the effective operation of a\nmunicipality and for the safety and well-being of the citizens of this\nstate. Volunteer firefighters and volunteer emergency services workers\nprovide an incalculable benefit to municipalities. Despite their\nimportance, the number of volunteer firefighters and volunteer\nemergency services workers has declined significantly over the past\nfew years. Therefore, it is the intention of this legislature to help\nrevive interest in serving as a volunteer firefighter or volunteer\nambulance worker.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS : None to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :  This act shall take effect on the 180th day.\n",
